{"name":"Kissed by Mist","hex":"#fcccf5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kissed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of kiss"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kissed"},{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kissed","blocks":[{"text":"Kissed is a 1996 Canadian romantic/erotic drama film directed and co-written by Lynne Stopkewich, based on Barbara Gowdy's short story \"We So Seldom Look on Love\". It premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival on September 7, 1996."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Kissed_%281996_movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kissed","wikidata":"Q939844"},{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mist","wikidata":"Q192196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_%28DanH-9388%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Barbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_%28DanH-9388%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_%28DanH-9388%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Barbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_%28DanH-9388%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"We So Seldom Look on Love\", a 1992 short story about a necrophile written by Barbara Gowdy (pictured) was Lynne Stopkewich's main inspiration for Kissed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_(DanH-9388)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/PER51895_061.jpg/500px-PER51895_061.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/PER51895_061.jpg/1280px-PER51895_061.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/PER51895_061.jpg/500px-PER51895_061.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 1974 film Effi Briest, directed by Rainer Werner Fassbinder (pictured), was an influence on Stopkewich's symbolic use of white light in Kissed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APER51895_061.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Chambord_au_lever_du_jour.jpg/500px-Chambord_au_lever_du_jour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Chambord_au_lever_du_jour.jpg/1280px-Chambord_au_lever_du_jour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Chambord_au_lever_du_jour.jpg/500px-Chambord_au_lever_du_jour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Château de Chambord in France, in mist","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChambord_au_lever_du_jour.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Morning_mist_-_panoramio_-_Henrik_Heino.jpg/500px-Morning_mist_-_panoramio_-_Henrik_Heino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Morning_mist_-_panoramio_-_Henrik_Heino.jpg/1280px-Morning_mist_-_panoramio_-_Henrik_Heino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Morning_mist_-_panoramio_-_Henrik_Heino.jpg/500px-Morning_mist_-_panoramio_-_Henrik_Heino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A light morning mist on Lake Suolijärvi in Hervanta, Tampere, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMorning_mist_-_panoramio_-_Henrik_Heino.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/American_Falls_and_Rainbow.jpg/500px-American_Falls_and_Rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/American_Falls_and_Rainbow.jpg/1280px-American_Falls_and_Rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/American_Falls_and_Rainbow.jpg/500px-American_Falls_and_Rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A rainbow formed from the water spray at American Falls","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi